WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.850
At the Ruins of the King's Tomb,
located in the northern lands

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.350
To the eighteen of you 
who passed the first test...

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:13.200
Second Test Proctor

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:13.200
Sense, First-Class Mage

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.190
First, congratulations on making it here.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:21.970
I hear people speculate all kinds of things 
about my tests based on past results.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:27.610
I'm sure there are some of you 
who have heard such rumors,

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:30.080
but you needn't prepare 
yourselves for the worst.

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:33.200
The test is very simple.

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:38.290
Anyone who wishes to become a first-class 
mage should be able to pass it with ease.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:44.050
Now, allow me to explain 
the details of the second test.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:58.030
You're there like the wind

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:02.660
Closing your eyes at sunset

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:08.290
I wonder what's on your mind

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:13.630
Beyond Journey's End

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:17.010
With your eyelids open

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:21.600
Your eyes shone like glass

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:28.350
It faintly smelled like a sunny day

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:39.490
Clear up the sky, let flowers bloom

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:43.700
Bloom and blame it on the sunny sky

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:48.080
Even the rain, when it stops

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:53.090
Will make you shine in the sunlight

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:58.470
Calm the stirring sounds in my heart

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:02.510
We go like the sunny wind

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:06.930
Go on and fly over that cloud

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:11.770
Further and further away

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.990
Episode 23: Conquering the Labyrinth

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.850
For the second test, 
you will be raiding a dungeon.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:26.110
You will raid the Ruins of the King's Tomb.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:33.880
There is only one condition for passing: 
you must reach the deepest floor of the tomb.

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:39.620
I am a pacifist. I dislike fighting.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:43.520
Therefore, everyone who reaches 
the bottom will pass.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:44.610
Wait.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:50.260
Many adventurers have failed to return 
from this unexplored dungeon.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:53.160
Are you planning to fail 
all the test-takers again?

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.510
What are you talking about?

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:59.410
You are attempting to reach 
the pinnacle of magehood.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.630
First-class mages make 
the impossible possible.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:09.010
You must forge ahead, regardless of whether 
or not anyone's been there before you.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:15.200
How should we prove we've reached the bottom?

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.000
Should we return with treasure?

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.480
You won't need to prove it.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.640
I will descend to the bottom 
of the dungeon with you.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:27.050
Naturally, I will not be 
assisting the test-takers.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:32.230
Also, each of you will receive 
one of these bottles.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:39.130
It's an escape golem developed 
by the first-class mage Lernen.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.800
When the bottle is shattered,

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.510
the golem will manifest 
and carry you out of the dungeon.

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:49.230
They're still prototypes, 
but they're safe enough.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.210
Using your bottle means you fail the test,

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:56.540
but I urge you to do so if you become unable 
to continue due to injuries or otherwise.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:00.650
I have no intention of allowing mages 
with promising futures to die here.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:06.480
Also, the bottles will shatter 
automatically at dawn tomorrow.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:10.010
That is the time limit of the second test.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.430
Now, let the test begin.

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:38.210
There are multiple entrances.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:41.500
This seems to be a dungeon 
of the Unified Dynasty.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:45.680
Dungeons of that era have multiple entrances,

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.510
but they all lead to the deepest level.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.720
Examining the entrances should allow us

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.760
to determine the internal 
structure of the dungeon.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:56.270
The group should split up and—

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:59.020
Why are you acting like 
we're working together?

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:08.020
There's no reason for us to fight this time.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:11.290
It's better for all of us to cooperate.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:13.550
I can't agree to that.

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:20.040
Unlike in the first test, our companions' 
survival isn't a condition for passing the test.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:23.540
We're not obligated to help each other,

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.550
and we even risk becoming someone's 
sacrificial pawn if the need arises.

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:32.040
You in particular seem 
knowledgeable about dungeons.

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:35.170
I'm going alone.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:52.160
We're all carrying baggage from the first test.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:55.820
At the very least, I can't work 
with anyone I don't know well.

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:00.260
Let's go.

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:04.400
Wait for me.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:13.670
Those fools. Why don't they realize 
working together is better?

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:15.830
Let's go, Fern.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.570
Are you sure, Ms. Frieren?

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:22.870
There's no chance of everyone 
working together anymore.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:29.940
I see.

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.920
I shall accompany your group.

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:38.950
You seem like you'll have the 
safest time reaching the bottom.

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:41.900
You'd better not interfere.

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:45.900
I shall neither interfere nor assist you.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.220
This is the safest route.

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:01.440
We'll proceed with caution 
while mapping the dungeon.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:17.540
The floor there is trapped. Be careful.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.580
You always know so much about dungeons.

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:30.140
I didn't always.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:33.880
It was Himmel who loved dungeons.

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:38.190
We entered so many of them 
to hunt down monsters.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:42.550
What do you mean, he loved dungeons?

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.070
It's exactly what it sounds like.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.340
He said they excited him.

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:50.050
It doesn't make sense, does it?

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:56.710
These stairs lead to the next floor.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:01.600
I see. Then we chose the wrong route.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:04.680
Let's head back to the last branch.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:06.060
Indeed.

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:11.900
Why? We're looking for the monster 
at the bottom of the dungeon.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:15.220
When will you learn, Eisen?

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:21.650
In a dungeon, one must explore the entire 
floor before proceeding to the next one.

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:23.620
Every adventurer knows that.

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:25.300
I've never heard that before.

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:29.240
You think I'm being foolish, don't you?

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:35.390
But isn't it best to be able to have fun 
while helping people?

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:38.300
It won't always be like this.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:41.080
As we travel, the dungeons will 
become more life-threatening.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:42.510
That's right.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.050
I intend to enjoy it until the end.

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:48.750
I'll have fun adventuring, raiding dungeons,

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.740
defeating monsters, finding treasure,

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:54.750
and before I know it, 
I'll have saved the world.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:58.490
That's the kind of adventure I want to have.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:01.180
Besides...

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:06.520
There might be a rare grimoire 
down the path left untraveled.

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:09.430
What are you doing? Let's hurry back.

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:10.530
What?

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:14.690
It really doesn't make sense, does it?

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:30.030
Kanne, let's go.

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:46.200
In the end, only the five of us stayed.

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:50.490
We could've beaten the dungeon easily

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:53.480
if we'd all worked together 
and assigned roles.

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:58.230
We had enough skilled mages to make it happen.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:02.870
Denken, not everyone is as pragmatic as you.

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:07.200
It's like what you said 
toward the end of the first test.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:12.740
It must not have sat right with them.

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:17.330
Think of it this way: 
only the smartest have remained.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:20.110
At the very least,

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:24.770
there aren't any idiots here to hold us back 
by falling for simple traps like mimics.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:27.260
Isn't that good enough, Denken?

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:31.670
I doubt anyone that foolish would 
be taking this test to begin with.

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:34.170
Let's go.

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:45.310
This mana...

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:48.000
It might be a grimoire.

00:10:48.530 --> 00:10:52.530
Ms. Frieren, you saw the results 
of that Mikheit spell.

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:55.350
It's a mimic.

00:10:56.430 --> 00:11:01.310
Fern, that spell is only 99% accurate.

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:03.430
And what if it is?

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:11.290
Historical discoveries have been made by 
great mages who recognized that remaining 1%.

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:18.190
It's just as I thought.

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:22.670
There's a valuable grimoire inside here.

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:27.600
That's what my experience 
as a mage is telling me.

00:11:33.390 --> 00:11:36.960
It's dark and scary in here!

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:39.840
It's dark! I'm scared!

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:42.850
It's dark and scary!

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:59.480
Maybe I chose the wrong people to follow.

00:12:09.070 --> 00:12:11.460
Don't step on the floor in the center.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.830
The ceiling will come crashing down on you.

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:19.910
Is that person-shaped stain there...

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:23.920
Brutal. It doesn't even leave bones behind.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:46.360
Gargoyles!

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:47.010
Denken, someone got trapped.

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:47.970
I know.

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:50.220
She's on the other side of the wall.

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:53.320
Stand back.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:01.810
It didn't work.

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:03.560
Then we have no choice.

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:05.310
Break your bottle!

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:23.710
Wow.

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:26.350
We're already down another test-taker.

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:32.840
Letting your guard down for a moment 
here could cost you your life.

00:14:34.460 --> 00:14:37.210
So these are the Ruins of the King's Tomb.

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:50.740
Hey, Fern. Can I make a suggestion?

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:54.250
Stop pulling. You're going to rip me in half.

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:55.780
Okay.

00:14:57.380 --> 00:15:01.140
To save someone from a mimic, 
you should push in instead.

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:04.040
It makes the mimic choke and stop biting.

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:07.880
Is it a dog or something?

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:13.060
I'm safe.

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:15.510
Honestly.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:19.020
How did you get out of those 
when you were by yourself?

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:22.220
By blowing them up from the inside 
with offensive magic.

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:26.900
But I don't like to do it 
since it makes my hair frizz up.

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:28.020
I'm back.

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:30.750
I have ringlets now.

00:15:31.400 --> 00:15:35.840
So that's why you'd sometimes 
have a different hairstyle.

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:36.840
Why?

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:42.530
Let's pull ourselves together and keep going.

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:52.090
Gargoyles.

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:54.580
We'll defeat them before they start moving.

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:01.850
We've been seeing these 
medals all over the place.

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:04.650
Apparently some dilettante collects them.

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:12.650
This looks like the main route. 
Let's turn back.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:13.540
Why?

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:19.940
We're progressing more 
smoothly than I expected.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:24.450
It does seem a bit odd 
for an unexplored dungeon.

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:27.690
Judging by its construction, 
we should be nearing the bottom, too.

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:30.940
Either way, don't let your guard down.

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:34.950
Let's take a break in the 
next burial chamber we find.

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:40.700
We've acquired some pretty nice stuff.

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:42.860
It just looks like junk to me.

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:44.850
Huh.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:50.200
I don't get it.

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:51.450
Neither do I.

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:54.890
Why do those things make her happy?

00:16:56.630 --> 00:16:58.150
She's rubbing it on her cheek.

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:03.040
You're the one I don't understand, Fern.

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:08.580
I've never seen a mage 
as skilled as you at your age.

00:17:09.150 --> 00:17:11.540
You must have trained rather hard.

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:15.680
And yet I sense no passion 
or determination in you.

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:17.080
You're a strange girl.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:26.430
I became a proper mage 
to repay a debt to someone.

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:32.440
That was my life's goal at the time.

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:35.180
I devoted all my effort to achieving it

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:38.460
without considering anything 
that would come after that.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:46.940
I must've used up all my passion 
and determination then.

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:52.600
Then why do you continue 
searching for magic?

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:58.590
Ms. Frieren seems to be 
having fun, doesn't she?

00:17:58.590 --> 00:17:59.730
Yes.

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:03.840
The first time I entered a dungeon,

00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:10.330
Ms. Frieren joyfully smiled 
while collecting magic junk.

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:17.780
It made me smile, too.

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:26.100
I think I continue searching for magic 
because I like seeing her happy.

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:31.860
We should get going.

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:40.550
Looks like I was right 
to follow you after all.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:46.060
I'm sure you can enjoy 
even this brutal dungeon.

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:12.020
The atmosphere has changed.

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:15.450
Maybe we're near the bottom.

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:19.280
Wirbel.

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:21.810
What? Can't walk any—

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:23.520
I'm restrained.

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:26.380
There are three mages concealing their mana.

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:27.890
It's an ambush.

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:29.020
Oh?

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:35.320
Scharf, block their vision.

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:37.940
The spell cast on Ehre is Sorganeil.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:38.990
I know.

00:19:54.490 --> 00:19:58.540
No wonder the Ruins of the King's Tomb 
have never been conquered.

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:04.110
I wasn't expecting to encounter these here.

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:07.310
Scharf, you're on me.

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:09.560
Ehre, you're on Scharf.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:11.850
And I'll take on Ehre.

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:14.950
Let's do this.

00:20:55.380 --> 00:20:58.970
It's a replica made using magic.

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:02.460
It must be the work of demons or monsters.

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:08.760
But I've never seen such a perfect copy 
of another person before.

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:12.270
Its mana and skills were 
the same as yours, Laufen.

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:14.960
So was its behavior.

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:18.370
It's possible even our memories were used.

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:21.670
I don't like this.

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:27.590
The one saving grace is that it's 
instantly recognizable as a fake.

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:31.900
At the very least, there's no danger 
of us attacking each other.

00:21:32.340 --> 00:21:38.030
If whoever cast this spell can control 
multiple copies simultaneously,

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:40.550
they must be terrifyingly powerful.

00:21:43.050 --> 00:21:47.190
Either way, we were right to team up.

00:21:50.730 --> 00:21:53.520
It gives us more options 
for dealing with them.

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:22.060
Denken, can we deal with that, too?

00:22:27.950 --> 00:22:32.770
The one thing I can say 
is that if this weren't a test,

00:22:32.770 --> 00:22:35.800
I would've shattered my bottle 
a long time ago.

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:53.140
And I'm alright (I'll be alright)

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:56.060
Yeah, I hear you (I care about you)

00:22:56.060 --> 00:23:01.650
The wind teases this hair that's longer now

00:23:01.650 --> 00:23:04.070
There's meaning in everything

00:23:04.570 --> 00:23:07.070
Even the days that came to a halt

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:13.700
Now that I finally understand,
I've caught up to you

00:23:13.700 --> 00:23:17.500
See, things that couldn't have been

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:20.370
Seen if it weren't for these eyes

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:25.050
Why? They begin to overflow

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:31.300
I won't ask to see you, so at least

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:37.060
Let me remember the past, just for today

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:43.060
So, if we were to meet again

00:23:43.060 --> 00:23:48.940
No more hesitations, I'd choose the present

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:52.990
Anytime, anywhere, yah (wherever you are)

00:23:52.990 --> 00:23:57.620
Anytime, anywhere (smile for me)

00:23:57.620 --> 00:24:00.620
I'll be there (close your eyes,
and I'll always be there)

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:03.380
Even if there are no absolutes

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:06.420
I'm always aware of your thoughts

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:12.470
Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break

00:24:12.930 --> 00:24:19.390
I'm whispering our lullaby
for you to come back home

00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:23.770
Now then, what are we going to do about this?

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:22.190
Smells nice.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:23.040
It's time.

00:24:22.320 --> 00:24:24.120
If we're evenly matched,

00:24:23.810 --> 00:24:25.000
That's not funny.

00:24:24.120 --> 00:24:26.260
then who wins will come down to luck.

00:24:24.310 --> 00:24:26.400
Could you please look into my eyes?

00:24:25.780 --> 00:24:27.670
So it's not impossible.

00:24:26.290 --> 00:24:28.100
How much time do you need?

00:24:27.520 --> 00:24:29.980
Episode 24







Perfect Replicas

00:24:28.100 --> 00:24:30.030
They're perfect replicas.
